WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now I thought I'd share
some of my favorite

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.803
"weirdest Halloween ever"
stories from you guys.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
This first one is from
@RealAmyJo.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.409
She says, "We rang the bell at
a house, and the guy was drunk.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.044 line:92%
He had no idea it was Halloween.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.078 line:92%
So he just gave us each a dollar

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then turned off
his porch light."

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.449 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.818 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"Am I a pretty emoji?"

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.821 size:84% position:42% line:92%
This one's from @cam31.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
He says, "Once at the mall,
I saw five people

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
walk into a public restroom
dressed as Clark Kent.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
Five minutes later,
all five of them came out

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.362 size:78% position:39% line:92%
dressed as Superman."

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Wow, they really planned it.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.568 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Look, it's five birds!

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
No.
They could be five drones."

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just update.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, update.
Just trying to make it modern.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.811
"I'm gonna call an Uber."
You're making it modern.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.913 line:92%
-Yeah, making Superman modern.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.581 line:92%
-This one's from @NatalieWild7.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.785
She says, "My friend and I were
walking through a haunted house

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:52.452 size:88% position:44% line:92%
when a clown jumped out.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
My friend freaked out and
screamed, 'Not today, biatch,'

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.723 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and then ran away."

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:59.559 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Why go?

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.263 line:92%
-Stay in your lane, clown.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Unh-unh!

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.567 line:92%
-This one's from @GumGummerson.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ol' Gum Gummerson!

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:14.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Old Gum Gummerson.
-I've been here many years.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:17.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got my prospectin' pan.
-Old Gum Gummerson.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:21.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
Man, get out of here, you --
-Dagnabbit!

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What's Gum say?

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:25.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gum says, "A trick-or-treater
once showed up at my door

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a poncho that had the name
John written on it.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.124
When we asked what he was,
he replied, 'I'm John.'"

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.759 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:33.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good costume.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.162 line:92%
-Then Gum gave him some gum.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.631 line:92%
-This one's from @MissLoriT.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, @MrsLoriT.
-Oh, Mrs.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.735 line:92%
-Maybe she's married to Mr. T.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:43.369 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She says --
-I pity the fool.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's that?
-I pity the fool.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.712 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Who's married to Mr. T.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.181
-The idea was that Superman
used to say, "It's a bird."

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"It's a plane.
It's Superman."

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
He didn't say it.
The people would say that.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, humans walking around
Metropolis.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:01.321 line:92%
-Right, would go, "Oh, my gosh,

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a bird, it's a plane,
it's Superman.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, it's a plane.
No, it's Superman."

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now you're saying,
"Is that a drone?"

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.530
-That's correct, or is that a --
some type of --

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Person.
-A flying --

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.501 line:92%
A remote-control flying thing?

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that some sort
of a flying device?

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Maybe Balloon Boy?

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:25.411
And so people say, "Is that
a drone or Balloon Boy?"

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.346 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No, by golly.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's just Superman.
-In fact, it's just Superman.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.818 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Yet again I was tricked.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:36.089
-You fooled me once again.
-You fooled me once again.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.792 line:92%
-Kryptoday and Kryptonite.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.428 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.166 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, my God.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:51.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whaa! Shwack.
Trick or treat.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
This one's from @PunkReckless.
-Yeah.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:58.711
-She says, "I was dressed
as a fortune teller at a party.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.712 line:92%
A guy asked me to read his palm,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I told him he'd get drunk
and have a good time.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:05.251
He came back an hour later,
told me I was the real deal.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.920 line:92%
Then he fell over a table."

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.656 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
This last one
is from @MattLong1.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
He says, "I once got so drunk
at a Halloween party

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.265 size:81% position:41%
that when I got home,
I egged my own house."

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.133 line:92%
There you have it, everybody.

